# CLOpts public symbol list: the single source of truth for the symbols the
# shared library exports (checked by the label-abi tests in tests/abi/).
#
# Format (UTF-8, LF):
#   - One symbol name per line, the same on every OS (no macOS leading "_").
#   - Names must match ^clopts_[a-z0-9_]+$ and must not be duplicated.
#   - Leading and trailing whitespace is ignored.
#   - Blank lines and lines starting with "#" (after optional whitespace) are
#     ignored.
#   - Order is free; by convention names are grouped per public header under a
#     "# clopts/<module>/<header>.h" comment, in the header's declaration
#     order, and the groups follow the modules (base, decl, parse, process,
#     text).
#   - Only CLOPTS_API functions are listed; static inline functions in the
#     public headers (e.g. clopts_file_write) are not exported and are not
#     listed.
#   - A name exported only on some OS carries one platform tag after it,
#     separated by whitespace. The only tag is "windows" (declared under
#     _WIN32; required only by the Windows export formats dumpbin and
#     objdump-pe, and wrapped in #ifdef _WIN32 by the C++ link check).
#     Any other tag, or more than two words on a line, is an error.
#
# Updating: a change that adds or removes a public (CLOPTS_API) function must
# update this list in the same commit. Add the name under its header's group
# at the position of its declaration, or remove it. A mismatch between this
# list and the exported symbols fails the abi tests; fix it by updating this
# list or by no longer exporting the symbol. See docs/dev/abi-checks.md for
# the full procedure.

